  28:Generated_Source\PSoC5/AMux_Capacitor.c **** *
  29:Generated_Source\PSoC5/AMux_Capacitor.c **** * \brief Writes the value to the physical port (data output register), masking
  30:Generated_Source\PSoC5/AMux_Capacitor.c **** *  and shifting the bits appropriately. 
  31:Generated_Source\PSoC5/AMux_Capacitor.c **** *
  32:Generated_Source\PSoC5/AMux_Capacitor.c **** * The data output register controls the signal applied to the physical pin in 
  33:Generated_Source\PSoC5/AMux_Capacitor.c **** * conjunction with the drive mode parameter. This function avoids changing 
  34:Generated_Source\PSoC5/AMux_Capacitor.c **** * other bits in the port by using the appropriate method (read-modify-write or
  35:Generated_Source\PSoC5/AMux_Capacitor.c **** * bit banding).
  36:Generated_Source\PSoC5/AMux_Capacitor.c **** *
  37:Generated_Source\PSoC5/AMux_Capacitor.c **** * <b>Note</b> This function should not be used on a hardware digital output pin 
  38:Generated_Source\PSoC5/AMux_Capacitor.c **** * as it is driven by the hardware signal attached to it.
  39:Generated_Source\PSoC5/AMux_Capacitor.c **** *
  40:Generated_Source\PSoC5/AMux_Capacitor.c **** * \param value
ARM GAS  C:\Users\elias\AppData\Local\Temp\ccR8ZMHH.s 			page 16


